WEBVTT

00:04:29.724 --> 00:04:32.435
but for me, I knew
it wasn't going to work.

00:04:32.476 --> 00:04:34.645
So I started to reference
well-being practices

00:04:34.645 --> 00:04:37.023
that I had learned from my own studies.

00:04:37.064 --> 00:04:39.191
Doctors always laugh with me

00:04:39.191 --> 00:04:43.404
when they find out that I'm a bio-psych
and neuroscience major

00:04:43.404 --> 00:04:45.072
and psych PhD student.

00:04:45.406 --> 00:04:47.158
Then when they ask what I'm studying

00:04:47.158 --> 00:04:50.453
and I tell them I study
resilience and well-being,

00:04:50.494 --> 00:04:53.122
they either laugh again,
say something like,

00:04:53.164 --> 00:04:54.957
"Oh, that's irrelevant,"

00:04:54.999 --> 00:04:56.667
or go, "Aw."

00:04:57.126 --> 00:04:59.378
The irony was never lost on me.

00:04:59.420 --> 00:05:02.715
I have read so many stories
and studies of resilience,